From: NomDeTom <nomdetom@protonmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] usb: cancel the stall watch again once no connect can start it

aicwf_bus_deinit() cancels the stall watch first, but the wiphy is
unregistered only later, in rwnx_cfg80211_deinit(). A connect in flight
between the two (an unload or a reset during a join) can have its
SM_CONNECT_CFM come after the cancel and start the watch again; its tick
then runs on a usbdev that is freed by then.

rwnx_cmd_mgr_quiesce() runs once wiphy_unregister() has returned, when no
connect can start, and still before the platform goes; it now cancels the
watch too. The cancel in aicwf_bus_deinit() stays: it stops the watch's
reads before the URBs are cancelled.
---
 src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_cmds.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_cmds.c b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_cmds.c
--- a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_cmds.c
+++ b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_cmds.c
@@ -907,6 +907,10 @@ void rwnx_cmd_mgr_quiesce(struct rwnx_cmd_mgr *cmd_mgr)
 {
     if (!cmd_mgr || !cmd_mgr->cmd_wq)
         return;
+#ifdef AICWF_USB_SUPPORT
+    /* Again, as aicwf_bus_deinit() did: a connect confirmed since may have started it. None can start now. */
+    aicwf_join_watch_cancel(container_of(cmd_mgr, struct aic_usb_dev, cmd_mgr));
+#endif
     spin_lock_bh(&cmd_mgr->lock);
     cmd_mgr->state = RWNX_CMD_MGR_STATE_DEINIT;
     spin_unlock_bh(&cmd_mgr->lock);
